1
00:00:06,690 --> 00:00:12,310
 1830, we're at Santa Marta, a small town in northern Colombia facing the Caribbean.

2
00:00:14,330 --> 00:00:18,170
 Forty years earlier in Caracas.

3
00:00:18,590 --> 00:00:21,020
 Oh, in the name of goodness, where's my caratom, mate?

4
00:00:21,080 --> 00:00:22,700
 The city is under Spanish rule.

5
00:00:22,960 --> 00:00:23,560
 At last.

6
00:00:26,580 --> 00:00:47,530
 Six years later, you have to awaken consciousness and understanding, my boy.

7
00:00:47,630 --> 00:00:50,450
 Unfortunately, our society is corrupt and not fit for men.

8
00:00:50,450 --> 00:00:53,530
 Yet, even in the days of Pericles, the ancient Greeks said,

9
00:00:53,650 --> 00:00:55,330
 man is the measure of all things.

10
00:00:56,650 --> 00:00:59,790
 You see, Simone, this country needs a radical change in society.

11
00:00:59,930 --> 00:01:03,550
 What we must have is a liberated society free of Spanish rule.

12
00:01:04,330 --> 00:01:06,490
 That one man be made to serve another is shameful.

13
00:01:06,650 --> 00:01:07,610
 No more of that, son.

14
00:01:07,930 --> 00:01:08,950
 No more and never again.

15
00:01:14,710 --> 00:01:17,690
 Your flowers are so beautiful, Simon.

16
00:01:17,790 --> 00:01:18,570
 You are very foolish.

17
00:01:18,770 --> 00:01:20,990
 What would I not do to please you, my dear Teresa?

18
00:01:21,500 --> 00:01:22,590
 What can I do?

19
00:01:22,690 --> 00:01:25,350
 Such a priceless pearl must also have a worthy setting.

20
00:01:25,950 --> 00:01:30,170
 Maria Teresa del Toro and Simon Bolivar lived on in intense happiness,

21
00:01:30,390 --> 00:01:31,390
 but it was short-lived.

22
00:01:32,100 --> 00:01:37,640
 Carried off by a terrible fever, she was to remain forever Simon's only great love.

23
00:01:39,740 --> 00:01:43,630
 18.4. Now we're in Paris.

24
00:01:45,500 --> 00:01:49,160
 We play the game of look-alikes, my friends.

25
00:01:49,660 --> 00:01:52,470
 And I suggest we start with Monsieur Beauharnais.

26
00:01:52,870 --> 00:01:55,130
 Tell us which animal Simon brings to mind.

27
00:01:56,400 --> 00:02:02,530
 Hmm. He's a strange bird. Every time I see him, I can't help thinking of a sparrow.

28
00:02:03,000 --> 00:02:04,190
 Exactly that, a sparrow.

29
00:02:04,400 --> 00:02:06,560
 Perfect. Inspiration.

30
00:02:06,560 --> 00:02:11,950
 A pecking bird. That is an insult, Monsieur. I won't allow it.

31
00:02:12,130 --> 00:02:13,470
 You will hear from my seconds.

32
00:02:13,850 --> 00:02:16,800
 Oh, my goodness, Simon, really, you can be short-tempered, all right?

33
00:02:16,980 --> 00:02:19,180
 I love it when you are like this, swift as lightning.

34
00:02:19,860 --> 00:02:22,560
 But you are quite wrong, I assure you, you misunderstand.

35
00:02:23,320 --> 00:02:25,590
 Here, we are all very fond of you, Simon.

36
00:02:32,450 --> 00:02:35,300
 Simon, Simon Rodriguez, you in Paris!

37
00:02:35,840 --> 00:02:39,350
 Hmm, well, Simon, you're so elegant, brilliant,

38
00:02:39,510 --> 00:02:42,290
 but a young man with your qualities is better things to do, you know.

39
00:02:42,750 --> 00:02:46,670
 There are higher callings than visiting Parisian ladies, no matter how beautiful.

40
00:02:47,390 --> 00:02:50,930
 More passionate pursuits like liberty and the liberation of our country.

41
00:02:51,710 --> 00:03:02,760
 How I did admire Bonaparte, the genius of liberty.

42
00:03:02,880 --> 00:03:05,500
 Now emperor he is, ah, truly the height of hypocrisy.

43
00:03:06,710 --> 00:03:10,350
 Sooner or later, all princes become tyrants and all power corrupts.

44
00:03:10,450 --> 00:03:12,290
 True, but a glory such as he had known.

45
00:03:12,570 --> 00:03:15,950
 We await the one who will deliver our beautiful land from bondage.

46
00:03:16,460 --> 00:03:18,950
 Tell me, Simon, whom do you see for this role?

47
00:03:19,190 --> 00:03:21,650
 Miranda, yes, only Miranda, no one else.

48
00:03:23,570 --> 00:03:26,250
 1810, it's a Bonaparte who reigns in Madrid.

49
00:03:26,470 --> 00:03:30,730
 Caracas, a junta, takes advantage of the situation to disrupt the Spanish forces.

50
00:03:32,330 --> 00:03:36,170
 And Simone, with the rank of colonel and elected official, is named head of mission,

51
00:03:36,550 --> 00:03:38,830
 sent to England to request aid.

52
00:03:39,520 --> 00:03:44,980
 But his deepest desire is to find his famous compatriot, Miranda, friend of high and mighty

53
00:03:44,980 --> 00:03:49,220
 Miranda, Spanish officer, Russian colonel, general of the French Revolution.

54
00:03:49,960 --> 00:03:53,740
 He's well-educated, oh yes, and a master of war.

55
00:03:54,610 --> 00:03:56,190
 This Francesco de Miranda.

56
00:03:56,310 --> 00:04:02,960
 Our great country is awakening to liberty, but the men who command our junta have had no experience.

57
00:04:03,100 --> 00:04:04,880
 Their mistakes will be costly to our cause.

58
00:04:05,320 --> 00:04:06,360
 We need a great leader.

59
00:04:08,640 --> 00:04:11,560
 General, will you hear your country's call and be that leader?

60
00:04:30,600 --> 00:04:32,720
 But disappointments were not long in coming.

61
00:04:32,900 --> 00:04:37,300
 The country is divided, ideas of joining together, and tolerance still have a long way to go.

62
00:04:38,280 --> 00:04:41,400
 Yet all the same, in July 1811...

63
00:04:41,400 --> 00:04:45,390
 The Congress declares unanimously the Republic of Venezuela free and independent.

64
00:04:45,490 --> 00:04:51,200
 The Spanish troops are everywhere in the country, and on the offensive, the people must defend themselves.

65
00:04:51,490 --> 00:04:55,390
 Is it an army such as this that a general of my stature must lead into battle?

66
00:04:56,070 --> 00:04:59,130
 Disappointed in his troops, bitter General Miranda will fight badly,

67
00:04:59,190 --> 00:05:02,170
 and in the end will ask the Spanish General Monteverde for an armistice,

68
00:05:02,510 --> 00:05:05,090
 which turns into capitulation in time.

69
00:05:06,070 --> 00:05:10,150
 Later, informing no one, General Miranda would get away by any means,

70
00:05:10,230 --> 00:05:12,590
 go to England, and leave this unworthy country.

71
00:05:13,470 --> 00:05:16,510
 Miranda is a coward? He's a traitor? Surely not.

72
00:05:16,510 --> 00:05:20,540
 Disgusted, yes, a man with a quick eye who could discern before others

73
00:05:20,540 --> 00:05:25,540
 the lack of maturity in his people in the face of great ideas of liberty and independence.

74
00:05:25,540 --> 00:05:26,540
 Where's the chief?

75
00:05:26,540 --> 00:05:32,660
 One moment, gentlemen, coming.

76
00:05:32,660 --> 00:05:34,660
 Your conduct has been unworthy, General Miranda.

77
00:05:34,660 --> 00:05:37,660
 We expect you to explain yourself. You are under arrest.

78
00:05:39,130 --> 00:05:42,510
 Words talk. That is all you are capable of.

79
00:05:42,510 --> 00:05:47,330
 And Miranda would end his days in prison.

80
00:05:47,330 --> 00:05:49,380
 As for Simon, after a number of tribulations,

81
00:05:49,380 --> 00:05:56,740
 tribulations, one fine day he's again commanding a garrison at Barranca, a community of no special interest, in the young Republic of

82
00:05:56,740 --> 00:06:07,140
 Carthagena. The garrison of 200 men isn't very enterprising. What in a very short time the young Colonel Bolivar is to

83
00:06:07,140 --> 00:06:15,010
 achieve with this handful of men is truly astonishing. You too. I'm counting on you to turn these men into soldiers. Get on

84
00:06:15,010 --> 00:06:27,860
 with it. One more thing. Wear proper boots. You understand? Slow, careful aim, then fire.

85
00:06:37,190 --> 00:06:53,940
 forward. Also built embarkation points. To the cheers of the crowd, they left the town

86
00:06:53,940 --> 00:07:01,640
 for Tenerife, where the Spanish flag was flying. Yes, the town was quickly taken. And then

87
00:07:01,640 --> 00:07:18,790
 they would cross the Andes. This is the city of Guenta, which in turn is going to be taken.

88
00:07:29,500 --> 00:08:07,920
 Salt on Merida. Advance continued. 6th of August, 1813, after marching over 2,000 kilometers,

89
00:08:07,920 --> 00:08:10,650
 fighting battle after battle without a single defeat.

90
00:08:10,650 --> 00:08:15,330
 After this admirable campaign, here is Bolivar with his men in Caracas.

91
00:08:15,330 --> 00:08:43,050
 The situation has changed considerably.

92
00:08:43,050 --> 00:08:46,090
 Wellington inflicted a stinging defeat on the French at Waterloo,

93
00:08:46,090 --> 00:08:51,050
 and Ferdinand's return to the throne is imminent.

94
00:08:51,050 --> 00:08:57,250
 The Spanish troops, backed up by reinforcements, were becoming aggressive,

95
00:08:57,250 --> 00:09:01,280
 and Bolivar has to strike hard to convince the undecided he had to be merciless.

96
00:09:01,280 --> 00:09:04,190
 Merciless war. That's my kind of war. I can't wait.

97
00:09:04,190 --> 00:09:07,930
 The Spanish commander, Monteverde, has just refused again to exchange prisoners, sir.

98
00:09:07,930 --> 00:09:10,370
 He says he refuses to deal with rebels.

99
00:09:10,370 --> 00:09:15,450
 The men continue to be tortured and even executed.

100
00:09:15,450 --> 00:09:18,970
 Under these conditions, kill all our Spanish prisoners, all we have.

101
00:09:18,970 --> 00:09:20,990
 That should make him think.

102
00:09:20,990 --> 00:09:22,720
 Oh.

103
00:09:22,720 --> 00:09:28,860
 A soldier, even when victorious, has no right to govern his country.

104
00:09:28,860 --> 00:09:31,870
 He is only the defender of her liberties.

105
00:09:31,870 --> 00:09:36,480
 Therefore, you must elect your representatives and the government of the land.

106
00:09:36,480 --> 00:09:46,060
 Do not burden me with an office I am not competent to hold.

107
00:09:46,060 --> 00:10:05,860
 The people insist I can only bow to their will.

108
00:10:05,860 --> 00:10:38,660
 battles among them are all infamous can't hold out much longer general the troops are starting to

109
00:10:38,660 --> 00:10:43,690
 desert we cannot allow ourselves to lose this battle colonel you bring up the rear with your

110
00:10:43,690 --> 00:10:49,160
 dragoons you others are to shoot any of our men running away from the battle deserters i'm counting

111
00:10:49,160 --> 00:10:56,990
 on you colonel i expect you to do your duty colonel cavalry with me charles this time once again it

112
00:10:56,990 --> 00:11:11,460
 was victory but bolivar's problems are far from over because allied with the spanish now is the

113
00:11:11,460 --> 00:11:16,190
 frightening bloodthirsty Boves, chief of the Leoneros, horsemen of the plains, Indians

114
00:11:16,190 --> 00:11:20,160
 and creoles, whose frustrations and misery he knew how to play on.

115
00:11:20,160 --> 00:11:26,480
 I told the whites, kill them all, the Indian persecutors, this land is ours!

116
00:11:26,480 --> 00:11:29,310
 Let's look magic at all of them, down to the very last one!

117
00:11:29,310 --> 00:11:48,260
 San Mateo, Bolivar and his troops are ready for battle, awaiting the expected attack of

118
00:11:48,260 --> 00:11:50,440
 Boves and his savage Leoneros.

119
00:11:50,440 --> 00:12:57,720
 The military at San Mateo will be short-lived, three months later facing the same Boves at

120
00:12:57,720 --> 00:12:58,750
 Puerta.

121
00:12:58,750 --> 00:13:00,030
 It will be a disaster.

122
00:13:00,550 --> 00:13:02,170
 Once again, all is lost.

123
00:13:07,640 --> 00:13:08,080
 1816.

124
00:13:10,520 --> 00:13:12,580
 In the name of all Republican Venezuelans,

125
00:13:12,580 --> 00:13:14,740
 I wish to thank you most warmly and sincerely

126
00:13:14,740 --> 00:13:16,020
 for all that you have done,

127
00:13:16,120 --> 00:13:17,800
 all the assistance given to our great cause,

128
00:13:17,900 --> 00:13:18,580
 President Petion.

129
00:13:18,840 --> 00:13:21,600
 Ah, but insofar as you seek to abolish slavery in our country,

130
00:13:21,700 --> 00:13:23,140
 it is quite fitting and proper

131
00:13:23,140 --> 00:13:25,670
 that I help you in any way possible, General Bolivar.

132
00:13:25,870 --> 00:13:28,420
 Thanks to President Petion's help,

133
00:13:28,540 --> 00:13:31,160
 Simon Bolivar is able to carry on the fighting.

134
00:13:34,880 --> 00:13:40,340
 I welcome you among us, General Payez.

135
00:13:40,400 --> 00:13:41,320
 I thank you, Liberator.

136
00:13:41,460 --> 00:13:46,280
 I can tell you since Boves' death, I have succeeded in turning his men into fervent Republicans.

137
00:13:47,000 --> 00:13:51,360
 Quite sure that together we will accomplish great things.

138
00:13:52,820 --> 00:13:55,120
 Look, an enemy garrison.

139
00:13:55,380 --> 00:13:57,160
 How do we get the army across, Paes?

140
00:13:57,340 --> 00:13:59,030
 We've only to make use of these boats.

141
00:13:59,520 --> 00:14:01,560
 All I will need is some 50 men.

142
00:14:21,260 --> 00:14:45,150
 Each and here we're 19 at Angostura, the very city where the Congress is being held.

143
00:14:45,150 --> 00:14:51,840
 The government of the Republic must rest upon the sovereignty of the people,

144
00:14:52,310 --> 00:14:56,300
 the separation of power, civil liberty, the abolition of slavery,

145
00:14:56,460 --> 00:15:01,900
 suppression of privilege yes our people have been under the yoke of ignorance and tyranny unable to

146
00:15:01,900 --> 00:15:08,450
 acquire knowledge or power or virtue your task will be difficult distinguished to the president

147
00:15:08,450 --> 00:15:14,000
 of the congress all my civil powers for my part i have decided to continue the struggle for the

148
00:15:14,000 --> 00:15:49,270
 republic's liberty against the oppressor some rain this will cool things off a bit like to introduce

149
00:15:49,270 --> 00:16:01,220
 my new chief of staff colonel santander general murillo is entrenched here with the spanish now

150
00:16:01,220 --> 00:16:06,780
 during the rainy season nobody ever attacks never and this is precisely what we'll do at tunja

151
00:16:06,780 --> 00:16:12,890
 this will open the way to bogota it's hundreds of kilometers here at tamay santander will arrange

152
00:16:12,890 --> 00:16:17,890
 a halting place you buyers will go along the river apuri and attack the enemy from the north

153
00:16:17,890 --> 00:16:24,270
 we gentlemen we will attack here where it's least expected this way cross the andes he's

154
00:16:24,270 --> 00:16:31,610
 gone crazy our leader we're going to cross the andes count on us general we'll follow you anywhere

155
00:16:34,620 --> 00:18:15,900
 Sickness, it's nothing.

156
00:18:15,900 --> 00:18:32,450
 Santander, true to his word, is waiting at the appointed spot.

157
00:18:32,450 --> 00:18:48,510
 "We shall clothe the naked, so said our lord."

158
00:18:48,510 --> 00:18:52,570
 "As you can see, these men who suffered to win our liberty are naked."

159
00:18:52,570 --> 00:18:56,560
 "And so, my brothers, you must clothe them now. Right now."

160
00:18:56,560 --> 00:19:20,420
 "Gift of this horse, General Bolivar, to thank you for fighting for our freedom."

161
00:19:20,420 --> 00:20:34,230
 "And boyar Bolivar, the waveta, the opulent."

162
00:20:34,230 --> 00:20:38,370
 "There, as acting vice president, he will leave General Santander."

163
00:20:38,370 --> 00:20:44,890
 "Other officer will return to Venezuela and report to the Angostura Congress."

164
00:20:44,890 --> 00:20:51,070
 I declare the states of Venezuela, Nu Granada, and Ecuador united under the name the Republic of Colombia.

165
00:20:51,070 --> 00:21:01,340
 And here is Bolivar fighting in Ecuador, ably assisted by General Sucre.

166
00:21:01,340 --> 00:21:08,160
 Yes, and this should be the triumphant entry to Quito, the capital where Bolivar is to meet a new passion.

167
00:21:08,160 --> 00:21:09,890
 Sanes.

168
00:21:09,890 --> 00:21:17,500
 At Guayaquil, he meets San Martin, the liberator of South America.

169
00:21:17,500 --> 00:21:22,810
 Iberador, I agree totally with your ideas of federating all the countries of your great continent.

170
00:21:22,810 --> 00:21:26,430
 But I fear that for the present, there is too much intrigue ambition.

171
00:21:26,430 --> 00:21:28,960
 No one has sufficient political maturity.

172
00:21:28,960 --> 00:21:34,110
 Then, Protector, it will be for future generations to complete our work.

173
00:21:34,110 --> 00:21:37,600
 But I am more than ever convinced that it is a grand and good idea.

174
00:21:37,600 --> 00:21:40,830
 In that case, since you are certain, I will abandon the task to you.

175
00:21:40,830 --> 00:21:57,570
 Il Bolivar moves toward Lima in Peru.

176
00:21:57,570 --> 00:22:02,170
 Victories in Hunin, and especially Ayacucho, which Sucre had masterminded,

177
00:22:02,170 --> 00:22:07,170
 brought the Spanish domination to an end, and this was soon to be replaced by Bolivar's rule.

178
00:22:07,170 --> 00:22:24,700
 -Simon Rodriguez! -You recognize me after 20 years.

179
00:22:24,700 --> 00:22:27,760
 Yes, the beard is longer, but yes.

180
00:22:27,760 --> 00:22:30,460
 For one thing, you're wearing the same clothes, aren't you?

181
00:22:30,460 --> 00:22:32,100
 I'm about to set off for the South.

182
00:22:32,100 --> 00:22:33,950
 You will come along with us.

183
00:22:42,310 --> 00:22:51,720
 You two friends, you will help me to build this Bolivia we have just founded.

184
00:22:51,720 --> 00:22:55,140
 You, Field Marshal Sucre, will be the first president.

185
00:22:55,140 --> 00:22:59,380
 As for you, my friend Simon, you'll be Minister of Public Education.

186
00:22:59,380 --> 00:23:03,180
 I suggest that our schools be co-educational, the sexes are equal.

187
00:23:03,180 --> 00:23:08,730
 And in this way, you young ladies will be able to prove to the boys that you're worth just as much as they are.

188
00:23:08,880 --> 00:23:13,620
 President, who is this visionary whom the Liberatore has given us to educate all our children?

189
00:23:15,360 --> 00:23:20,100
 In the time's jackasses, they are living in a past century.

190
00:23:20,200 --> 00:23:23,500
 Very well, since that is how they want it, you can get along without me.

191
00:23:23,720 --> 00:23:24,280
 I'm leaving.

192
00:23:25,650 --> 00:23:31,710
 But with the impetus of the ambitious Vice President Santander, Simon's fortunes changed.

193
00:23:32,260 --> 00:23:36,240
 The Congress at Bogota would relieve him of his command over the forces.

194
00:23:36,240 --> 00:23:39,560
 and everywhere throughout the country there is vaulting ambition.

195
00:23:41,330 --> 00:23:44,490
 I will be the future president. Me, me, me.

196
00:23:45,470 --> 00:23:47,930
 Very soon I shall be the new president, yes.

197
00:23:48,670 --> 00:23:52,940
 It will be me, the one, the president.

198
00:23:54,540 --> 00:23:56,220
 Dissension rages in Bogota,

199
00:23:56,420 --> 00:24:00,040
 and once again the Congress has to call on the man for all seasons.

200
00:24:00,790 --> 00:24:02,170
 Simon, my brother.

201
00:24:02,690 --> 00:24:04,790
 Simon, my friend, welcome to you.

202
00:24:04,870 --> 00:24:06,910
 I am so very glad to see you again.

203
00:24:10,850 --> 00:24:43,780
 Simone, my friend, I'm so pleased that you escaped that dastardly attempt on your life.

204
00:24:45,170 --> 00:24:49,310
 The traitor who organized this plot, General Santander, is condemned to death.

205
00:24:50,430 --> 00:24:54,650
 No, no, not a death sentence for a man who fought courageously for his country.

206
00:24:55,540 --> 00:24:57,260
 And the best man of the continent.

207
00:24:58,430 --> 00:24:59,700
 No, the best man is me.

208
00:25:00,120 --> 00:25:01,430
 No, no, I am the one.

209
00:25:02,010 --> 00:25:03,730
 Of course not, I am the best.

210
00:25:03,850 --> 00:25:04,870
 Apparently I'm not needed.

211
00:25:06,060 --> 00:25:08,770
 I relinquish all this power that you so covet.

212
00:25:08,950 --> 00:25:10,950
 Manage yourselves, but as for me, I am leaving.

213
00:25:11,380 --> 00:25:15,620
 Simon was hoping that once again they would call him back, but it wasn't to be.

214
00:25:16,410 --> 00:25:20,430
 Alas, I believe we have only one hope, if the country's not to plunge into chaos.

215
00:25:21,700 --> 00:25:23,910
 My son, my brother, Sucre.

216
00:25:24,170 --> 00:25:25,990
 Liberator, liberator, liberator.

217
00:25:26,460 --> 00:25:29,210
 Marshal Sucre's just been assassinated.

218
00:25:29,970 --> 00:25:37,350
 Who would serve a revolution is plowing the sea, my son.

219
00:25:38,490 --> 00:25:40,000
 Plowing the sea.

220
00:25:42,430 --> 00:25:47,590
 Always on the move, covering thousands and thousands of kilometers,

221
00:25:49,670 --> 00:25:53,990
 Simon Bolivar pritted his time away, gathering honors and glory.

222
00:25:53,990 --> 00:25:59,010
 In fact, the foundation of his power was shaky, and he had gathered a number of Brutuses around him.

223
00:25:59,290 --> 00:26:05,880
 When the man who wanted to unite all of Latin America died at 47, the region had no fewer than 16 countries.

